From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Subject: amdv: apply the target-luminance overrides in the multi_control_path site too

Patch 0001 added amdv_target_min_override / amdv_target_max_override and
wired them into the two p_funcs_stb->control_path call sites. Patch 0006's
comment then stated the override "still wins when Kodi sets it explicitly
(see the ternaries at the control_path call sites below)".

That is false on this hardware, and the overrides have never taken effect.
The shipped CMv4.0-generation dovi.ko exports ONLY multi_control_path -
there is no `control_path` symbol in the module at all (verified with nm on
5.15_2.6_dovi_patched_fix_fel.ko). The registration code takes the
`else if (func->multi_control_path && !p_funcs_stb)` branch and sets
multi_dv_mode = true, so the LIVE per-frame call is the multi_control_path
site, where set_target_min_lum / set_target_max_lum were assigned straight
from amdv_target_min / amdv_target_max[][] with no override ternary. Both
legacy control_path call sites are unreachable on any box running this
module generation.

Net effect before this patch: Kodi's DM target min/max settings (the VS10
target.minlum and display.maxnits levers, written via
aml_dv_apply_target_overrides) were silently discarded. Patch 0006's change
to the amdv_target_min DEFAULT did apply - only the override was dead.

Mirror the same ternaries at the multi site and correct the stale comment
so it points at all three call sites. Behaviour is unchanged whenever the
override params are 0 (their default, and what Kodi writes for bypass and
native-DV output).

--- a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
@@ -392,8 +392,9 @@
  * crush below code ~80 - for every VS10 conversion that doesn't set
  * amdv_target_min_override. 1 (0.0001 nit) keeps the floor at code ~65,
  * one step above reference black; amdv_target_min_override still wins
- * when Kodi sets it explicitly (see the ternaries at the control_path
- * call sites below).
+ * when Kodi sets it explicitly (see the ternaries at all three control
+ * path call sites below - the two legacy control_path ones and the
+ * multi_control_path one, which is the only live site on a CMv4.0 ko).
  */
 static unsigned int amdv_target_min = 1; /* 0.0001 */
 static unsigned int amdv_target_max[3][3] = {
@@ -10768,13 +10769,21 @@
 	new_m_dovi_setting.set_graphic_min_lum = graphic_min;
 	new_m_dovi_setting.set_graphic_max_lum = graphic_max * 10000;
-	new_m_dovi_setting.set_target_min_lum = amdv_target_min;
+	/* amdv_target_min/max_override (patch 0001) must win here too: this is
+	 * the only control-path call site a CMv4.0 dovi.ko ever reaches, since
+	 * such a module exports multi_control_path and no control_path.
+	 */
+	new_m_dovi_setting.set_target_min_lum =
+		amdv_target_min_override ? amdv_target_min_override : amdv_target_min;
 	if (vd_path == VD1_PATH || !vf) {//only update for vd1
-		if (src_format < 0  || src_format >= ARRAY_SIZE(amdv_target_max))
+		if (amdv_target_max_override)
+			new_m_dovi_setting.set_target_max_lum =
+			amdv_target_max_override * 10000;
+		else if (src_format < 0  || src_format >= ARRAY_SIZE(amdv_target_max))
 			new_m_dovi_setting.set_target_max_lum =
 			amdv_target_max[FORMAT_SDR][dst_format] * 10000;
 		else
 			new_m_dovi_setting.set_target_max_lum =
 			amdv_target_max[src_format][dst_format] * 10000;
 	}
 	new_m_dovi_setting.input[IPCORE2_ID].video_width = dv_cert_graphic_width;
 	new_m_dovi_setting.input[IPCORE2_ID].video_height = dv_cert_graphic_height;
